WEBVTT

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.060
What should I wear?

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.060
Right...

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.900
Maybe this.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.770
Hey, Yuu.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.990
Oh, good morning.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.600
You really want to waste 
your day off lying around?

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.510
Don't you have anyone to go on a date with?

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.940
Sh-Shut up!

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.600
I was just about to message the girls 
and ask if they all want to go shopping.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:45.420
What about you? Don't you have a 
girlfriend to go out with on your day off?

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.390
Don't worry about me.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.270
Oh, they responded.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:51.190
Let's see...

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.440
<b>Yuu</b>

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.440
<b>Bored (>□<)
Let's do something!!!!!</b>

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.440
<b>Jun</b>

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.440
<b>Sure.
Where should we go?</b>

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.440
Sweet, Jun's in.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:58.370
I wanted to invite Koizumi-san too,
 but I don't know her contact info.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.210
Not that she would ever tell me.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:02.750
Huh?

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.250
<b>Sorry, can't make it today.
Going on a date in Inogashira Park~
>▽<</b>

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.250
Huh? A date?!

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.250
<b>Misa</b>

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.490
I always knew Misa was popular, but still...

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.600
Wait, does she have a boyfriend right now?

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:14.970
Oh, well...

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.970
I wonder if Koizumi-san is eating 
ramen somewhere again today.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:39.450
<b>Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:39.990
<b>Ms. Koizumi</b>

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:40.910
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:56.030
<b>Hokkyoku</b>

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.240
Sorry, but I think you should break up with me.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:02.540
Huh?

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.990
I mean, you're very popular,

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.520
so even when we're together, 
I always feel uneasy.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.000
I just can't fully enjoy being together.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.360
You don't need to be with someone like me.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.960
There are so many great guys out there.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.870
Well, see you around.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:21.380
Hey, wai—

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.620
No! This can't be happening!

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:31.290
Me? Being dumped? When we 
haven't even held hands yet?

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.280
That was my first time dating someone,

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.730
<b>The type who never gets asked out
because people think
someone as cute as her
must have a boyfriend already</b>

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.730
and the first time someone 
told me they liked me!

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.490
You told me you liked me!

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:43.020
Why?!

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:47.680
Hey, hey!

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:49.720
Are you alone?

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.620
Wanna go get some food with us?

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.770
No!

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:55.180
Oh, come on.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.700
There's a nice little café over there.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.440
What's up?

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.010
That girl over there is cuter.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.160
You're right.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.060
<i>Koizumi? What's she doing here?</i>

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.850
Hey, cutie!

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:14.270
<i>Why's she wearing her school 
uniform on a day off?</i>

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.270
So...

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.830
Wanna grab some lunch?

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:16.730
No, thank you.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:20.900
<i>I really hope she didn't just 
see me getting dumped!</i>

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.340
<b>Mongolian Tanmen</b>

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.340
<b>Nakamoto</b>

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:45.970
<i>Ramen?</i>

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:48.970
<i>She's eating ramen alone?</i>

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.600
<i>She's not meeting someone here?</i>

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.600
<b>Spicy and Delicious Ramen   Best in Japan</b>

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.600
<b>Our No. 1 Menu Item</b>

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.600
<b>Mongolian Tanmen</b>

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.980
Welcome!

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.900
Um, could you please not stare at me?

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:20.640
Oh, Koizumi-san, what a coincidence!

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.770
I just came in to eat here myself.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:23.590
It <i>is</i> lunchtime.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.700
Who are you?

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.010
That's how you start?!

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.460
We're in the same class! I'm Nakamura Misa!

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.820
I don't want to be friends,
but at least remember my name!

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:33.800
Excuse me...

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:34.220
What?!

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:36.350
Please buy your food ticket first.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.400
Food ticket?

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.180
I have no idea what you're talking about!

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.610
Extra noodles, mini mabo rice bowl, rice, egg, oolong tea, extra roast pork

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.610
<b>Special Item Limited to Kichijouji
Hokkyoku in Spring</b>

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.610
Pick one

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.610
<b>Student Special</b>

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:46.770
The menu has so many options, 
I don't know what to get.

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.540
Excuse me, sir!

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:49.490
Yes?

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.990
<b>Hokkyoku Ramen</b>

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.990
<b>One</b>

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.990
<b>Total</b>

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.990
<b>One</b>

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.990
<b>yen</b>

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.990
<b>Mongolian Tanmen Nakamoto</b>

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:55.490
I didn't let him stop me.
I picked the ultra spicy one!

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:58.260
Even though they don't usually 
let newcomers order that.

00:05:58.260 --> 00:05:59.260
Are you sure?

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:00.000
Huh?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.750
This is your last chance 
to change your order.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.670
Why would I do that?

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.480
Hokkyoku has a spiciness level of nine.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:14.680
<b>H
o
k
k
y
o
k
u
 
R
a
m
e
n</b>

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:11.010
It happens to be this 
restaurant's final boss.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:13.310
<b>M
i
s
o
 
T
a
n
m
e
n</b>

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:13.060
<b>Gomoku
Mongolian
Tanmen</b>

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:12.810
<b>Mongolian
Tanmen</b>

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:14.680
It might be prudent to advance 
through the levels in order.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:19.510
I should tell you that it took me 
an entire year to get to level nine.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.920
It's that hot, huh?

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.460
Well, I happen to like 
spicy food, so I'll be fine.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.670
I've had a stressful day, so I'm 
in the mood for something hot.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.470
<b>Actual
Spicy
Food
Maniac</b>

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:36.880
Hey... Are you even listening?!

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:37.910
Don't ignore me!

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:43.890
Anyway, isn't it kinda sad for a high school girl 
to be out eating ramen alone on a day off?

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:45.590
Aren't you here alone, too?

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:48.590
I was with someone else until 
just a little while ago!

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.840
You mean the guy who dumped you?

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.600
Crap, you saw that?

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:55.250
Only by chance.

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:57.760
If you tell anyone at school, 
I'll tear you apart!

00:06:57.760 --> 00:06:59.980
I can't have anything 
tarnishing my popular image!

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.310
I have no reason to tell anyone.

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:06.200
<i>She's the last person I'd want to see that.</i>

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.780
Here you go.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:09.820
Here's your Hokkyoku ramen.

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:13.710
And here's our Hokkyoku ramen 
special student bonus with boiled egg

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:15.330
and an extra side of butter.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:18.240
It's so red! What <i>is</i> this?

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.220
Time to eat.

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:19.910
Huh?

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:22.550
What's that white stuff on yours?

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:23.920
I thought we had the same thing.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:26.920
This is a limited edition special.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:30.360
The regular Hokkyoku with 
cheese melted on top.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:33.200
Instead of pork, it has chorizo.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:37.390
However, the extreme spiciness 
of the soup and chopped chilies

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.310
overwhelms the spiciness of the chorizo.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.880
The cheese makes the spiciness a bit milder.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:48.380
Additionally, the boiled egg and 
butter further reduce the spiciness.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:55.670
You're sweating and tearing up!

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:57.080
You've only had one bite!

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:01.750
Extreme heat is not my forte.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.750
<b>Still
Delicious</b>

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:05.300
Then why are you eating 
this super spicy ramen?

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.670
I'm going to eat, too!

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:13.040
Time to eat!

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:17.890
Ouch!

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.940
My mouth is in pain!

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:23.890
My tongue is, like, th-th-throbbing!

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:23.890
<b>Told you so.</b>

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:30.650
But... I like it.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.080
I love this!

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:36.660
It's perfect for me!

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.720
So... spicy...

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:28.750
This was the first time anyone ever 
told me that they liked me to my face.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:32.500
It made me so happy.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:36.430
It...

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:41.380
Too spicy.

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:45.690
<b>Warning: Hokkyoku ramen 
is extremely spicy!!</b>

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.510
Thank you!

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:03.470
That was satisfying.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:04.640
It's hot.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:05.760
Hey, Koizumi.

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:08.040
Wanna give me your info?

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:11.400
I was thinking you could tell me about some 
other good places to have spicy ramen.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:12.790
I could really get into this.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:16.980
I-I'm not saying I want to go with you!

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:19.590
I'll find a new boyfriend and go with him!

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.220
I don't care one way or the other.

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:24.800
I think I could handle even spicier.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:27.700
You can ask them to
make it five times spicier.

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:28.560
Are you serious?

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:33.290
Yuu?

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.440
Huh?

00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:37.720
Why?

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:41.220
Why are the two of you together?

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:43.450
You told me you had a date today, Misa.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.700
Um, well, this is...

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.750
Misa, you traitor!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.090
Why do you get to be her friend before I do?!

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:54.680
Yuu, you can be so annoying!

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:56.580
Stop shouting.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:57.800
I'm going home.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:58.760
Huh?

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:02.210
Koizumi-san!

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:05.510
<i>I didn't think we'd run into each other here.</i>

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:06.590
<i>Oh, no...</i>

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:08.520
<i>This is too soon!</i>

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:13.020
<b>Spicy</b>

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:13.020
<i>Ah, that's spicy.</i>

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.020
<b>Cup
Noodles</b>

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.030
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:23.030
<b>K-K-K-K-Koizumi-san</b>

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:30.790
<b>2nd: Takahashi Jun</b>

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:32.330
Jun, that's amazing!

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:33.740
Uh, yeah...

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:36.100
That's our class rep!

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:42.310
<i>I wish they'd stop calling me that.</i>

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:44.670
<i>I only agreed to do it because 
everybody else refused.</i>

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:44.670
Yay!

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:47.220
No supplementary exams for me!

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.600
<b>91st:  Nakamura Misa</b>

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.600
Safe by a hair!

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.980
You're right, that <i>is</i> rare—

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:53.940
<b>91st:  Nakamura Misa</b>

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:57.820
<b>— Required Supplementary Exams —

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:55.440
What?!

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:57.820
Koizumi-san's on the list
for supplementary exams?!

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:01.020
No way!

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:01.810
I knew it.

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:02.950
Hey, Koizumi.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:07.210
What's that, Koizumi? You failed? 
Gotta take supplementary exams?

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.260
You poor thing.

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:15.930
You know, a girl can't just be pretty.
She also has to have <i>substance</i>.

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:16.840
You're just so...

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.840
How dare you ignore me?!

00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:22.760
That's strange.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.990
She placed pretty high on the 
entrance exams to transfer here.

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:27.170
Really?

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:29.720
How did you find that out?

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.600
Oh, Takahashi-san...

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.740
What is it, Sensei?

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:38.020
I need to talk to you about Koizumi-san.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.000
Bliss...

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.080
So this is where you always eat lunch.

00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:59.090
Isn't it a little cold today?

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:00.480
Why don't you eat inside?

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.990
Yuu's been looking for you.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:03.050
<b>Where are you?</b>

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:03.090
Where are you?

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:05.000
Koizumi-san!

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.550
<b>Koizumi-san!</b>

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:05.930
That's exactly why.

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:08.790
I generally prefer to be alone.

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:10.240
I see.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:12.260
I'm sorry I bothered you.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:15.180
Do you need something?

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:20.730
Our teacher told me that you handed in the 
last exam answer sheet completely blank.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:21.870
Is that true?

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:25.490
Is something weighing on you?

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:30.740
Our teacher asked me to have 
a talk with you, as the class rep.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:39.130
But yeah, if you don't want to 
talk about it, that's fine, too.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:42.420
I'll come up with something to tell the teacher.

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:45.130
Well, actually...

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:48.680
I was on a trip until 
the day before the exam.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:50.680
To the Tohoku region.

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:57.660
Unfortunately, my trip home was 
delayed due to inclement weather.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:14:00.840
<i>All trains have been canceled 
due to inclement weather.</i>

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:04.400
<b>Iwate</b>

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.220
<i>I guess I'll stay here another night.</i>

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:08.820
After all that, I did manage to get 
back to Tokyo on the day of the test.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:09.070
<b>Local
ramen
gifts</b>

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.910
<b>So heavy...</b>

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:13.510
I somehow made it to school, although late,

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:12.830
Ding
Dong

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:15.820
but I couldn't withstand my 
exhaustion and drowsiness.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.370
<b>Begin working
on the history exam</b>

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.370
<b>Zzz</b>

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:16.910
<b>Num
Num</b>

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:20.480
By the time I realized it, the test was over.

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:23.170
That's why I handed in my answer sheet blank.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:25.900
You took a trip?

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:27.420
Right before the exam?

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:28.620
Why?

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:36.900
I had the uncontrollable urge to eat 
natto kimchi cream cheese ramen.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:40.230
Natto? Cream cheese?

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:41.960
Is that any good?

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:42.720
It is.

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:43.940
I like it.

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:47.120
It's a special treat I always try to enjoy

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:50.450
when I'm in Iwate, along 
with reimen and jaajaamen.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:54.580
<i>She went all the way to Tohoku for that, 
right before an important exam?</i>

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:57.030
<i>I can't comprehend that.</i>

00:14:57.030 --> 00:15:00.870
<i>And today, too, she's eating 
some kind of strange ramen.</i>

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:03.040
<b>Pineapple Flavor
Salt Ramen
</b>With Fruit Chunks

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.540
<i>What's with the pineapple?</i>

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:09.030
So you're into... unusual 
flavors of ramen, huh?

00:15:09.030 --> 00:15:11.160
Since the beginning of the year, I've had

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:14.050
many opportunities to eat soy sauce 
ramen, the gold standard flavor,

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:14.050
<b>The number of good
soy sauce ramens
in the Minowa area!</b>

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:17.240
<b>Pineapple Ramen
P-P-P-P-Pine</b>

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:15.960
so perhaps as a reaction to that,

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:21.420
I've been really interested in the more 
uniquely crafted flavors lately.

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:23.810
That's also why I took my trip.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:27.610
Uniquely crafted ramens?
Are there even that many flavors?

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:33.180
One example is the chocolate ramen and tsukemen 
you can find a lot of around Valentine's Day.

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:36.740
In summer, tsukemen shops will have 
ice cream ramen and lemon ramen.

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:38.940
You can even find nuts and strawberries.

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:42.120
There are many limited edition 
varieties using seasonal ingredients.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.760
That's a pretty "Why would you 
combine these flavors?" line-up.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.620
Surprisingly, these are quite exquisite.

00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:51.950
By the way, this cup ramen 
is a bit of a treasure.

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:54.580
They have a restaurant here in the city.

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.140
You should really try it.

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:58.950
<i>Fruit in ramen, huh?</i>

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:01.240
<i>I guess it's kind of intriguing.</i>

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:03.140
Well, the truth is...

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:07.150
I don't like ramen.

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:11.740
I'm not saying I hate it, exactly,
 but there's a reason behind...

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.660
<i>She's so far away.</i>

00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:17.780
She suddenly put all this distance between us.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:22.540
I apologize for boring you with this topic.

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:24.410
No, that's not it.

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:26.840
Listen, don't run away!

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:29.670
If that was all, I'll be leaving now.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.170
Uh, sure...

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.170
<i>Oh, jeez.</i>

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:35.430
<i>I messed this up.</i>

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:37.300
Koizumi-san!

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:39.800
I'll help you study for 
your supplementary exams!

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:42.030
I can come along, too.

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:44.660
If you insist, that is.

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:45.440
No, thank you.

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:46.510
Come on!

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:48.190
You're so cold!

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:53.280
<i>I think I gave Koizumi-san the wrong idea.</i>

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:56.050
<i>I don't hate ramen or anything.</i>

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:58.830
<i>In fact, I even used to like it.</i>

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:04.540
<i>Wait, what was that one she was eating?</i>

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:06.540
<i>Pineapple ramen...</i>

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:07.540
<b>We actually put
pineapple in ramen!</b>

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.540
<b>Sour Meets 
Sweet</b>

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:07.540
<b>It... It's good!</b>

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:09.750
<i>There really is a restaurant.</i>

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:11.460
<i>And it's on the way home.</i>

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:13.090
<i>Close to my house, even.</i>

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:23.980
<b>Pineapple</b>

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:23.980
<i>This is the place, huh?</i>

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.980
<b><i>P-P-P-P-Pine</i></b>

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:27.990
<i>It's been a while since 
I've been at a ramen shop.</i>

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:29.980
<i>I used to avoid these places,</i>

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:34.990
<b>Since we love both 
pineapple and ramen,
isn't it okay to
put pineapple
in ramen?</b>

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:34.990
<b><i>Pineapple Ramen Shop
P-P-P-P-Pine</i></b>

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:34.990
<i>but talking to Koizumi-san gave me 
this intense craving for ramen.</i>

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:36.940
Surprisingly, these are quite exquisite.

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:39.010
By the way, this cup ramen 
is a bit of a treasure.

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:42.240
<i>I never thought she'd be that talkative, either.</i>

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:42.240
They have a restaurant here in the city.

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:45.250
<b>P-P-P-P-Pine's Favorite
Pineapple-Flavored Egg  100 Yen</b>

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:45.250
<b>Pineapple Beer</b>

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:45.250
<i>That's quite the menu.</i>

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:54.550
<b>Pineapple Shrimp Salt Ramen</b>

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:57.550
Welcome.

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:04.780
<i>This is... a ramen place, right?</i>

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:06.890
Thank you for waiting.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:08.040
Here you go.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:10.020
One order of pineapple shrimp salt ramen.

00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:14.490
<i>It's really got pineapple in it.</i>

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:16.530
<i>Can I even eat this?</i>

00:18:17.810 --> 00:18:21.530
<i>Good thing I got this scrunchie 
at the 100 yen store.</i>

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.160
<b>Right</b>

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.540
<i>Time to eat.</i>

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:41.550
<i>Wait, I really do... like this.</i>

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:43.970
<i>Soft-boiled egg.</i>

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:47.860
<i>I love these.</i>

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:52.890
<i>This is dangerously good.</i>

00:18:52.890 --> 00:18:55.590
<i>You can totally smell the pineapple.</i>

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:59.490
<i>It's almost like eating a dessert.</i>

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:04.240
<i>It's been so long since I had ramen.</i>

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:08.430
<i>It's so good. I can feel it warming me up.</i>

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:11.540
Welcome.

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:16.840
<b>Shrimp Salt Ramen</b>

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:22.260
I thought you said you 
don't really like ramen.

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:29.060
I don't.

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:31.460
I mean...

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.060
it always fogs up my glasses.

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:37.290
That's all?

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:38.820
What do you mean, "that's all"?!

00:19:39.180 --> 00:19:41.400
Last time I had ramen in the cafeteria,

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:43.760
this happened to me in front of everyone.

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:45.920
Class Rep, your glasses are totally white!

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:50.040
Everyone laughed at me,
and it was really embarrassing.

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:54.120
I've been avoiding hot 
noodle soups ever since.

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:56.040
I never hated them, though.

00:19:56.470 --> 00:19:58.790
Why don't you take off your 
glasses while you eat?

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:00.380
I can't see anything then!

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:02.220
You shouldn't mock super bad eyesight!

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:07.400
Ah, that was good.

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:09.470
Koizumi-san!

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:12.560
Thank you for telling me 
about this great place.

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:14.100
It's no problem.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.270
I'll be going now.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:20.530
Koizumi-san, see you tomorrow!

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.790
How'd you do on your supplementary exam?

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:28.140
I passed it.

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:31.430
By the way, the ramen from yesterday 
can be had in Machida, as well.

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:32.300
I see.

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:35.040
When did you two become friends?!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.050
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:30.030
<b>Saimin</b>

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:30.030
<b>Flavor Concentration Counter</b>

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:30.030
<b>Instant Noodles</b>

00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:17.480
Ugh, I can't believe it was 
Koizumi who saw me get dumped!

00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:20.520
What was she doing there, anyway?

00:22:21.130 --> 00:22:23.680
Maybe she was following me!

00:22:23.680 --> 00:22:26.300
I've been singled out as an enemy! Marked!

00:22:26.300 --> 00:22:27.360
It was a coincidence.

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:29.220
I won't be fooled!

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:36.040
<b>Thank you for the meal!</b>
